<title>POLAND: Poland cuts 10-yr bond min price, sells PLN 181 mln.</title>
<headline>Poland cuts 10-yr bond min price, sells PLN 181 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland cut the minimum price of its 10-year floating rate bond to 98.51 from 99.53 at the last auction on December 10, 1996, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>At today's 600 million zloty primary tender banks bid for 191 million of the bonds and the treasury accepted 181 million zlotys. The average price fell to 98.60 from 99.62.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
